be the matrix that represents the stretching, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the shearing, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =RQP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd2b79a-bc49-5c01-9237-4642e237863f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of an Object Under a Combination of Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3db33d1-0ade-5d29-ae78-283a10f19dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/933/Source/Images/q-70642-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090984} {:answer/id #uuid "10762cf5-f1b7-557b-bc9e-93702f1515a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/933/Source/Images/q-70642-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090985} {:answer/id #uuid "185ee500-14c5-5551-ab3c-7d2ca841ea3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/933/Source/Images/q-70642-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090986} {:answer/id #uuid "33f420d0-05e1-5c46-92ef-036d8c036586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/933/Source/Images/q-70642-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090987